---
title: Random rooms
---
Scatter rectangles over a solid map, keep the ones that don’t overlap, and join them with corridors [[t:47-51 s:5]].

## The rule
1. **Repeat 20 times** [[c01:21]]:
   1. pick a random rectangle [[c01:22-27]];
   2. if it overlaps or touches a room already placed, discard it [[c01:28-38 c01:47-53]];
   3. otherwise carve it as a room [[c01:40-46]].
2. Sort the rooms by their left edge [[c01:57]].
3. Join each room to the one before it, center to center [[c01:67-78]]:
   - a corridor of two runs, one across and one up or down [[c01:72-76 c01:85-101]];
   - a coin flip picks which run comes first [[c01:71-76]].

@@diagram rooms-join alt="A solid map with two rooms. A corridor runs right from the first room’s center, then down into the second room’s center. A third rectangle that touches the second room is marked as rejected." caption="A rectangle that touches a room is discarded (small squares). Two rooms are joined center to center by one run across and one down (marked tiles)."
